    {
      "path": "/training-samples/finance/",
      "status": 200,
      "structure": {
        "lang": "en",
        "title": "Reading a profit and loss statement: an eight minute module",
        "h1Count": 1,
        "headings": [
          {
            "level": 1,
            "text": "The profit and loss statement, read like an owner"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Before you start"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "What you will do"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "The statement, top to bottom"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Margin is the number"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "The worked example"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Move the levers"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Prompt one: find a price and a volume that pay for the month"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Prompt two: move cost of goods by five points"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Classify the line"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Flour, butter, and the bakery boxes"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "The store manager’s salary"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "A new deck oven, bought outright for $18,000"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Rent on the second location"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Paying back $1,400 of the amount borrowed for the oven"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "The owner taking $3,000 out of the business for herself"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Fuel for the van that runs bread to the wholesale accounts"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Everything rung up at the counter on a Saturday"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "The card processor’s fee on every counter sale"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "The bread still on the shelf when the month ends"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "Profit is not cash"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "One: a customer who pays in forty five days"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Two: flour sitting in the storeroom"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Three: a year of insurance paid in one month"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Add the three together"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "The decision"
          },
          {
            "level": 2,
            "text": "The margin check"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "The month as a chart"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "Three quick reads"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "1. What is the gross margin on this month?"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "2. Which single bar takes the most away from revenue?"
          },
          {
            "level": 3,
            "text": "3. Cost of goods rises five points, to forty five percent of revenue. "
